Picking clinic software is a decision you will live with every day. These are the questions we suggest asking any vendor, including us.\
\
Adios vamos!!

## 1. Who owns the data?

You should be able to export every patient record, including original documents, at any time and in a format another system can read.

## 2. Does it fit your front desk, not just the doctor?

Most delays happen at registration and in the queue. Ask to see walk-ins, follow-ups and queue reordering in a live demo.

## 3. How are permissions handled?

Receptionists, nurses and doctors need different access. Look for role-based access and an audit trail of important actions.

## 4. Can you move your existing records?

Ask how patients and history are imported from Excel or your current software, and how duplicates are caught.

## 5. What happens after go-live?

Training for every role, a named contact for support, and a clear way to raise issues on WhatsApp, phone or email.

## 6. Does it talk to patients?

Reminders and follow-ups through official business channels reduce no-shows without extra staff work.

## 7. Are the claims real?

Ask which certifications have actually been obtained. A good vendor will tell you plainly what is and isn't in place.

## The short version

Choose software that your whole team will use, that keeps your data yours, and whose vendor answers these questions clearly. If you'd like to see how NuvaLyf answers them, [book a demo](/book-a-demo).
